course: dictionary
lesson: 15130
title: Satisfying: pleasure and meeting a need
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A word can have more than one meaning, so look at the words around it. «The jigsaw was finished at last, and it was very satisfying.» The clue is that the puzzle is finished and done well, so satisfying means giving you a happy, pleased feeling.
explain: Satisfying can also mean meeting a need or a rule. «Hungry Sam ate a big bowl of soup, which was satisfying.» The soup met his need to feel full. In maths, «a number satisfying x + 3 = 7» is one that makes the sum true: 4 + 3 = 7, so 4 satisfies the equation.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping in a simpler word. «The soup was pleasing» still makes sense for Sam, so the meaning fits. When a maths word is new, test the number in the equation and see if both sides match.
fact: Satisfying means giving you a feeling of pleasure because something is done well.
fact: «A satisfying meal» is one that fills you up and makes you feel content.
fact: Satisfying can also mean meeting a need or a rule, as in maths.
fact: In maths, a number that satisfies an equation makes it true.
fact: Satisfying is the -ing form of the verb satisfy. Its comparative is more satisfying and its superlative is most satisfying.
exercise: «Finishing the puzzle felt very satisfying.» What does satisfying mean here? | *Giving a happy feeling because it was done well | Very difficult to do | Boring and slow | Making a loud noise
exercise: «Sam ate a big bowl of soup, which was satisfying.» What does satisfying mean here? | *Filling, so Sam's hunger was met | Lost in the bowl | Cold and sticky | Hot and spicy
exercise: Which number satisfies the equation n × 2 = 10? | 2 | *5 | 8 | 20
test: Which number satisfies x + 3 = 7? | 3 | *4 | 10 | 7
test: «The bubble wrap popping was very satisfying.» Which word is most like satisfying here? | Frightening | Sleepy | Heavy | *Pleasing
exam: Which number satisfies 5 + x = 9? | 3 | 5 | 14 | *4
